ole-based restrictions."},{"kind":"permission","text":"The app presents only the requests list and request detail screens; attempts to use capabilities outside the specified request operations are not provided."}],"id":"I-1"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"On initial setup, the app provides exactly 8 valid requests: 4 Open (including one Urgent), 2 In progress, and 2 Done."},{"kind":"data","text":"Across the seed records, every supported area (Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, Reception) appears at least once."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Creating additional requests is allowed; the count of eight applies to shipped seed data, not a runtime limit."}],"id":"I-2","readingChosen":"“Ships with exactly 8 requests” means the initial seeded data contains eight requests; it is not a cap on requests users may create."},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"data","text":"After a request is created successfully, its data remains available after the page is reloaded and after the application or database is restarted."},{"kind":"data","text":"After a status change succeeds, the new status remains in effect after reload and restart."},{"kind":"error","text":"A failed create or status change does not persist the rejected data or status."}],"id":"I-3"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"The API supports listing all requests or filtering the list by one status; results are newest first, and a status-filtered response contains only matching requests."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The API supports creating a request. It accepts a title of 3–80 characters, a supported area, a supported priority, and an optional description of at most 500 characters; it assigns the ID and creation date and starts the request as Open."},{"kind":"error","text":"A create request with a missing or invalid required field, a title outside the allowed length, or a description over 500 characters is rejected with an error identifying the field; no request is created."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The API supports retrieving one request by ID; an unknown ID is reported as not found."},{"kind":"error","text":"The API supports changing status only along Open → In progress, In progress → Done, and Done → Open. Any other requested transition is rejected and leaves the status unchanged."},{"kind":"permission","text":"The API exposes no other request operations: clients cannot edit request fields after creation or delete requests."}],"id":"I-4"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"The requests screen initially selects All and lists every request newest first. Selecting Open, In progress, or Done selects that filter and displays only requests with that status; only one filter is selected at a time."},{"kind":"happy","text":"While the list is being retrieved, the screen displays “Loading requests…”. If the selected filter has no results, it displays “No requests here.”"},{"kind":"error","text":"If loading the list fails, the screen displays “Could not load requests.” and a Retry button; retrying attempts to load the list again."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The New request button opens a dialog with labeled Title, Area, Priority, and Description fields; Priority defaults to Normal. Cancel closes the dialog without creating a request."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Submitting valid values creates an Open request; on success the dialog closes and the new request appears at the top of the list."},{"kind":"error","text":"Submitting an invalid title, missing or unsupported area or priority, or a description longer than 500 characters keeps the dialog open and shows the relevant field error beneath that field."},{"kind":"error","text":"While a create request is being sent, Create is disabled; repeated or double clicks do not create duplicate requests."}],"id":"I-5"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Opening a request displays its title, area, priority, status, created date, and description; when the description is absent it displays “No description.” A Back link returns to the requests screen."},{"kind":"happy","text":"For an Open request, the action is Start work; for In progress, it is Mark done; for Done, it is Reopen. After a successful action, the displayed status and action button reflect the new status."},{"kind":"error","text":"If a status update fails, the screen displays “Could not update the request.” and continues to show the previous status."},{"kind":"error","text":"Opening an unknown request ID displays “Request not found.” and a link back to the requests screen."}],"id":"I-6"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"The screens use a light theme with a neutral background, near-black text, one brand color for primary buttons, and a sans-serif font; there is no dark-mode option."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Status badges show both text and color: Open is blue, In progress amber, and Done green. Urgent priority is red; Low and Normal are neutral."},{"kind":"happy","text":"At 375 px width, request rows stack as cards; at 1280 px width, they display as a table. The page has no horizontal scrolling at these widths."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Every field has a label, all controls can be reached and used with a keyboard, and text meets WCAG AA contrast."},{"kind":"happy","text":"The top bar shows the Hive Works wordmark and Sam Carter’s initials, SC."}],"id":"I-7"},{"behaviours":[{"kind":"happy","text":"Automated business-rule tests verify that a valid request is created as Open; missing or too-short title, missing area, and overlong description are rejected; all three allowed status transitions succeed; and a disallowed transition is rejected."},{"kind":"happy","text":"Automated tests verify that status-filtered lists contain only matching requests and are newest first, and that an unknown ID is reported as not found."},{"kind":"happy","text":"An end-to-end test opens the list, creates a request, verifies it appears at the top, opens it, starts work, marks it done, selects the Done filter, and verifies the request is listed there."}],"id":"I-8"}]}]